1
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:03,378
HELLO.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,588
Chandler:
Hey, it's me.

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,256
You can't stand
to be in the same room as me

4
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:07,633
so I thought I'd apologize

5
00:00:07,675 --> 00:00:09,510
over the phone. All...

6
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:14,055
( rings )

7
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,433
HELLO.

8
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:18,435
Chandler:
Look, I never should have...

9
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:19,520
and I'm...

10
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:23,482
( ringing )

11
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:24,817
STOP CALLING!

12
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:27,194
( Chandler as deejay ):
Hey, hey, hey!

13
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:29,196
This is 92.3 WXRK, K-Rock

14
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:31,740
calling with our $1,000
daily challenge.

15
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:33,074
ALL RIGHT.

16
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:35,076
What is the name
of your roommate

17
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:38,455
who is very, very sorry
and would do anything...?

18
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:49,925
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

19
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:52,427
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

20
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:54,805
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

21
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:59,768
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

22
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:02,229
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

23
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,982
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

24
00:01:05,024 --> 00:01:07,735
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

25
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,987
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

26
00:01:10,029 --> 00:01:12,656
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

27
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:15,116
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

28
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:18,412
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

29
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:24,585
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

30
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:30,257
UGH... TURKEY.

31
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:32,634
UGH, GIVING THANKS.

32
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:33,969
UGH!

33
00:01:34,011 --> 00:01:35,054
LOOK, EVERYONE.

34
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:37,222
IT'S THE SPIRIT
OF THANKSGIVING.

35
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:39,182
SO, ARE THINGS
WITH YOU AND JOEY ANY BETTER?

36
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:40,517
THEY COULDN'T BE WORSE.

37
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:42,811
I SPENT EIGHT HOURS
CALLING HIM LAST NIGHT

38
00:01:42,853 --> 00:01:44,479
TRYING TO GET HIM
TO TALK TO ME.

39
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:45,898
OH, WOW.

40
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:48,442
EIGHT HOURS-- SO, YOU
COULD PROBABLY REALLY USE

41
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:51,028
ONE OF THOSE PLUG-IN
TELEPHONE HEADSETS, HUH?

42
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,321
SHOULD WE ALL EXPECT
CHRISTMAS GIFTS

43
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,699
THAT CAN BE STOLEN
FROM YOUR OFFICE?

44
00:01:58,035 --> 00:01:59,411
YOU SHOULDN'T.

45
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,456
SPEAKING OF CHRISTMAS

46
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:04,875
SINCE MONICA AND I
ARE STARTING A NEW BUSINESS

47
00:02:04,917 --> 00:02:06,293
AND HAVE, LIKE, NO MONEY

48
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:08,963
UM, THIS YEAR MAYBE
WE COULD DO SECRET SANTA

49
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:10,965
AND THEN WE EACH
ONLY BUY ONE GIFT

50
00:02:11,006 --> 00:02:13,216
AND-AND THERE'S
THE ADDED MYSTERY

51
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:14,969
OF, YOU KNOW,
WHO GETS WHO.

52
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,221
WHO GETS WHOM.

53
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:22,017
I DON'T KNOW
WHY I DO THAT.

54
00:02:25,813 --> 00:02:27,606
OH, I'M GOING
TO TAKE A NAP.

55
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:29,190
TURKEY MAKES ME SLEEPY.

56
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:31,234
WE HAVEN'T
EATEN YET.

57
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:33,821
I KNOW, BUT ALL THAT WORK
YOU'RE DOING

58
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,739
TO GET IT READY AND I JUST...

59
00:02:35,781 --> 00:02:37,240
HEY, BY ANY CHANCE

60
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,867
DID EITHER OF YOU
PICK RACHEL

61
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,160
FOR YOUR SECRET SANTA?

62
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:41,912
'CAUSE I WANT
TO TRADE FOR HER.

63
00:02:41,954 --> 00:02:42,913
I PICKED HER.

64
00:02:42,955 --> 00:02:44,456
OOH, THANK GOD, YOU WANT HER.

65
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:45,874
OOH!

66
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:48,335
WOW. WHY DO YOU WANT TO GET
RID OF HER SO BADLY?

67
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,879
BECAUSE SHE EXCHANGES
EVERY GIFT SHE EVER GETS.

68
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:53,423
IT'S IMPOSSIBLE TO GET HER
ANYTHING SHE LIKES.

69
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:54,842
COME ON, LET'S TRADE!

70
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:56,135
OH, THAT'S NOT TRUE.

71
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:58,095
I GOT HER THAT BACKPACK,
AND SHE LOVED IT.

72
00:02:58,137 --> 00:02:59,596
I REMEMBER HOW MUCH
SHE WAS CRYING THE DAY

73
00:02:59,638 --> 00:03:02,850
THAT BIG DOG
RAN OFF WITH...

74
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:05,060
WELL, THERE WAS
NO BIG DOG.

75
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:08,105
ALL RIGHT, THIS SUCKS

76
00:03:08,147 --> 00:03:09,773
'CAUSE I ALREADY GOT HER
THIS BRIEFCASE, AND I HAD

77
00:03:09,815 --> 00:03:11,859
"R.G." PUT ON IT.

78
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,694
HER INITIALS.

79
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,029
OH.

80
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,697
MAYBE YOU
CAN GIVE IT

81
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:17,990
TO SOMEBODY ELSE.

82
00:03:18,032 --> 00:03:19,533
OH, LIKE ROSS GELLER.

83
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:20,993
OH, YOU KNOW
WHAT, THOUGH?

84
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:22,744
IT'S KIND OF A
GIRLY BRIEFCASE.

85
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:24,997
WHO CARES?
HE WORKS IN A MUSEUM.

86
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,708
HEY, WHAT TIME IS IT?

87
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,877
THE BIG GAME IS
ABOUT TO START.

88
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:31,252
ROSS AND JOEY AREN'T HERE.

89
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:33,212
YOU CAN WATCH THE PARADE
IF YOU WANT.

90
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,589
THANKS.

91
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:38,052
WHAT IS WRONG
WITH THIS FREEZER?

92
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:39,803
OW! OW!

93
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:40,971
GOD, WHAT HAPPENED?

94
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:41,889
OH, MY GOD,
ICE JUST GOT

95
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,557
IN MY EYE!

96
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:46,101
PEOPLE ARE TRYING
TO SLEEP IN HERE.

97
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:48,395
MONICA GOT ICE
IN HER EYE,
AND IT HURTS.

98
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:49,688
OPEN IT UP.
LET ME SEE.

99
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,398
OH, I CAN'T.
IT REALLY KILLS.

100
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:52,774
WELL, MAYBE YOU SHOULD

101
00:03:52,816 --> 00:03:54,275
PUT SOME ICE
ON IT.

102
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,777
OOH, IT
LOOKS BAD.

103
00:03:55,819 --> 00:03:58,822
HONEY, MAYBE WE
SHOULD TAKE YOU
TO A DOCTOR.

104
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:00,365
NO. MY EYE DOCTOR IS RICHARD.

105
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:02,868
I CAN'T GO TO HIM
WHEN I DON'T HAVE A BOYFRIEND.

106
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:05,871
HE'S REALLY PICKY
ABOUT HIS PATIENTS.

107
00:04:05,913 --> 00:04:07,789
OKAY, YOU'VE GOT TO GO.

108
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,917
WHAT'S HIS OFFICE NUMBER?

109
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:13,003
LIKE, I REMEMBER
HIS OFFICE NUMBER.

110
00:04:13,045 --> 00:04:14,546
SPEED DIAL SEVEN.

111
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:20,761
HI. YEAH, I'M CALLING ON BEHALF
OF MONICA GELLER'S EYE, AND...

112
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:23,097
IS, UM...
IS RICHARD BURKE IN TODAY?

113
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:27,184
HE'S OUT OF TOWN, BUT DOES SHE
WANT TO SEE THE ON-CALL DOCTOR?

114
00:04:27,226 --> 00:04:28,018
YES!

115
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,937
YES! SHE'S VERY EXCITED

116
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:31,105
ABOUT THAT.

117
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:34,649
THIS IS SO COOL.

118
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:36,276
TILL MONICA GETS BACK

119
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:38,112
IT'S, LIKE,
I'M HEAD CHEF

120
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:40,781
AND I GET TO MAKE
ALL THE DECISIONS.

121
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:42,950
HEY, HEY,
I THOUGHT
SHE TOLD YOU

122
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,952
TO FOLLOW
THE RECIPE
EXACTLY.

123
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:47,495
OKAY, GET
OUT OF MY KITCHEN.

124
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:50,582
ALL RIGHT, I THINK I AM MAKING
SOME PROGRESS WITH JOEY.

125
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:52,251
WHEN I WENT
INTO THE APARTMENT

126
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,002
HE WENT STRAIGHT
INTO HIS BEDROOM

127
00:04:54,044 --> 00:04:55,879
BUT HE ONLY SLAMMED
THE DOOR ONCE.

128
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:57,131
WOW.

129
00:04:57,172 --> 00:04:58,506
I MEAN, YEAH, HE GAVE ME

130
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:00,050
THE FINGER WHILE DOING IT.

131
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:02,803
ALL RIGHT, I'VE...
I GOT TO CALL MY MOM

132
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,722
AND ASK HER
A LEFT-HANDED COOKING QUESTION.

133
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:12,520
SO, LISTEN, UH, I PICKED MONICA
FOR SECRET SANTA

134
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:14,231
BUT I'M ALREADY GETTING HER
SOMETHING FOR HANUKAH.

135
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:15,983
I WAS WONDERING
IF YOU WANT TO SWITCH.

136
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:17,151
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

137
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:19,486
I WAS TRYING TO TRADE
FOR, UH... WELL, YOU.

138
00:05:21,989 --> 00:05:22,781
REALLY?

139
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:23,907
WOW, THAT'S... THAT'S SO NICE.

140
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:24,950
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO GET ME?

141
00:05:24,992 --> 00:05:26,076
I DON'T KNOW, R.G.

142
00:05:26,118 --> 00:05:28,078
I THOUGHT SOMETHING GIRLY
FOR YOUR OFFICE.

143
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,330
YEAH.

144
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:33,458
WELL, MAYBE PHOEBE
WILL SWITCH WITH ME.

145
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:34,793
YOU DON'T WANT
TO DO THAT.

146
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:35,961
YOU'LL GET STUCK
WITH RACHEL.

147
00:05:36,003 --> 00:05:38,379
SHE EXCHANGES
EVERY GIFT SHE GETS.

148
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:39,547
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

149
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:41,340
I GOT HER LOTS
OF STUFF SHE
NEVER TOOK BACK.

150
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:42,050
LIKE?

151
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:43,384
LIKE THAT GOLD NECKLACE

152
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:44,719
I GOT HER LAST YEAR.

153
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:46,847
WHEN WAS THE LAST TIME
SHE WORE IT?

154
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:51,852
WELL, SHE WORE IT ALL
CHRISTMAS DAY, AND THEN, UH...

155
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,561
BIG DOG?

156
00:05:57,565 --> 00:05:58,859
HI.

157
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,194
HEY.

158
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,736
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

159
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:04,405
SENDING BACK THIS STUFF
CHANDLER BOUGHT OUT OF GUILT.

160
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:06,241
EVERYTHING?
EVEN THE TV?

161
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:08,743
NO. I'M GOING TO PUT THAT
IN MY ROOM.

162
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:11,163
LISTEN, JOEY...

163
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:13,165
I KNOW WHAT
HE DID WAS WRONG

164
00:06:13,207 --> 00:06:14,499
BUT DON'T YOU THINK

165
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,543
YOU COULD AT LEAST
HEAR THE GUY OUT?

166
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:19,004
BACK WHEN YOU AND RACHEL
WERE TOGETHER

167
00:06:19,046 --> 00:06:20,755
IF CHANDLER HAD KISSED HER

168
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,007
WOULD YOU
HEAR HIM OUT?

169
00:06:22,049 --> 00:06:23,342
GOOD POINT.

170
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:26,594
SO, UH, HOW LONG ARE YOU
GOING TO PUNISH HIM?

171
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:28,347
FIVE YEARS.

172
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:30,598
YOU'VE SENTENCED HIM?

173
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,810
HEY, DON'T DO THE CRIME
IF YOU CAN'T DO THE TIME.

174
00:06:33,852 --> 00:06:35,979
JOEY, THE GUY IS
YOUR BEST FRIEND.

175
00:06:36,021 --> 00:06:37,564
WAS MY BEST FRIEND.

176
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:40,317
ANYWAY, I DON'T KNOW WHY YOU'RE
PUSHING FOR HIM SO HARD.

177
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:42,694
WITH HIM OUT OF THE WAY
AS MY BEST FRIEND

178
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:44,154
THERE'S A SPOT OPEN.

179
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:47,241
WELL, WHO, ME?

180
00:06:47,282 --> 00:06:48,992
YEAH.
( chuckling )

181
00:06:49,034 --> 00:06:49,993
WOW. I'M HONORED.

182
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:51,245
YOU KNOW WHAT I'LL DO

183
00:06:51,286 --> 00:06:53,288
AS MY FIRST ACT
AS YOUR BEST FRIEND?

184
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,122
WHAT?

185
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:55,916
I'M GOING TO GET YOU

186
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,667
TO TALK
TO CHANDLER.

187
00:06:57,709 --> 00:06:59,502
ALL RIGHT.

188
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:02,421
OH, BUT IF YOU WEREN'T
MY BEST FRIEND...

189
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:03,798
YEAH...

190
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:07,135
OH, MY GOD. IS IT
REALLY THAT BAD?

191
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:10,055
I WALK INTO THE ROOM,
AND HE WON'T EVEN TALK TO ME.

192
00:07:10,097 --> 00:07:13,725
HE'LL JUST MUMBLE
SOMETHING IN ITALIAN...

193
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:17,187
AND I KNOW HE ONLY
KNOWS THE BAD WORDS.

194
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:22,317
HEY, GUNTHER,
HAVE YOU, UH...

195
00:07:22,359 --> 00:07:23,777
HAVE YOU SEEN
CHANDLER?

196
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,904
I THOUGHT
YOU WERE CHANDLER.

197
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,951
BUT, UM, ONE OF YOU
IS OVER THERE.

198
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:38,499
OH.

199
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,501
HEY, JOE.

200
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:43,546
VA FA A NAPOLI, HUH?!

201
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:51,346
I'LL BE RIGHT WITH YOU, OKAY?

202
00:07:51,388 --> 00:07:52,680
THANKS FOR COMING IN.

203
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:53,681
SURE.

204
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:55,642
OH, MY GOD.

205
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:58,145
HOW CUTE IS THE
ON-CALL DOCTOR?

206
00:07:58,186 --> 00:08:00,521
OH, SO CUTE
THAT I'M THINKING

207
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:03,150
ABOUT JAMMING THIS PEN
IN MY EYE.

208
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:04,484
( intercom buzzes )

209
00:08:04,525 --> 00:08:06,653
DR. BURKE WILL SEE YOU NOW.

210
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:07,988
OH, NO, NOT DR. BURKE.

211
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:09,323
DR. BURKE'S
OUT OF TOWN.

212
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:11,199
THE ON-CALL DOCTOR
WILL SEE ME NOW.

213
00:08:11,241 --> 00:08:13,368
DR. RICHARD BURKE
IS OUT OF TOWN.

214
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:16,330
DR. TIMOTHY BURKE, HIS SON,
WILL SEE YOU NOW.

215
00:08:17,372 --> 00:08:19,374
READY?

216
00:08:25,339 --> 00:08:27,341
HEY, I'M SORRY.

217
00:08:27,382 --> 00:08:28,675
THAT...

218
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:30,677
WHERE YOU GOING?

219
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,346
MY FOLKS'.

220
00:08:32,387 --> 00:08:35,849
OH. UH... WHEN YOU,
WHEN YOU COMING BACK?

221
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,184
I DON'T KNOW.

222
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:39,394
I MIGHT STAY THERE
FOR A FEW DAYS

223
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:41,396
WHILE I LOOK
FOR AN APARTMENT.

224
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:42,897
WHAT?

225
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:45,275
AT FIRST I THOUGHT
WE COULD TALK ABOUT THIS

226
00:08:45,317 --> 00:08:46,609
YOU KNOW, WORK IT OUT

227
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:48,778
BUT SEEING YOU TWO
TOGETHER AND ALL...

228
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,071
HEY, LOOK,
WHAT DO YOU

229
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:51,281
WANT ME TO SAY?

230
00:08:51,323 --> 00:08:52,573
DO YOU WANT ME

231
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,201
TO SAY I'LL
STOP SEEING HER?

232
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,869
IT'S NOT ABOUT HER, OKAY?

233
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:59,122
BUT SEEING YOU TWO TOGETHER
JUST REMINDS ME OF WHAT YOU DID

234
00:08:59,164 --> 00:09:02,125
AND I DON'T WANT TO LIVE
WITH SOMEONE WHO DOESN'T KNOW

235
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,752
WHAT IT IS TO BE A FRIEND,
SO I'LL SEE YOU.

236
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,381
LOOK, I KNOW WHAT IT IS
TO BE A FRIEND.

237
00:09:07,422 --> 00:09:09,007
I JUST... I SCREWED UP.

238
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:10,717
YEAH, YOU DID...

239
00:09:10,758 --> 00:09:13,053
AND THAT'S WHY
I'M LEAVING.

240
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,388
( quacking )

241
00:09:14,429 --> 00:09:15,347
ALL RIGHT, LOOK.

242
00:09:15,389 --> 00:09:16,348
IF YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO STAY FOR ME

243
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:18,392
THEN AT LEAST
STAY FOR THEM.

244
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:22,562
OKAY, THEY HAVE HAD
A VERY DIFFICULT YEAR

245
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:24,439
WHAT WITH THE ROBBERY AND ALL.

246
00:09:24,481 --> 00:09:25,857
WHEN THAT GUY
WAS ROBBING US

247
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:28,026
AND I WAS LOCKED IN
THE ENTERTAINMENT UNIT

248
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:29,403
FOR SIX HOURS,
DO YOU KNOW

249
00:09:29,444 --> 00:09:31,446
WHAT I WAS DOING IN
THERE ALL THAT TIME?

250
00:09:31,488 --> 00:09:33,573
I WAS THINKING ABOUT
HOW I LET YOU DOWN.

251
00:09:33,614 --> 00:09:34,574
WOW.

252
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:35,909
YEAH, BUT IF
I'D KNOWN

253
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,328
WHAT KIND OF FRIEND
YOU WOULD TURN OUT TO BE

254
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:40,621
I WOULDN'T HAVE WORRIED
SO MUCH ABOUT IT.

255
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:41,622
SEE YOU AROUND.

256
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:43,124
JUST WAIT
ONE SECOND NOW.

257
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:45,960
THERE HAS TO BE SOMETHING
THAT I CAN DO, SOMETHING.

258
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,837
IF WE STILL HAD
THAT ENTERTAINMENT UNIT

259
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:49,548
I WOULD GET IN THERE
FOR SIX HOURS AND THINK

260
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,591
ABOUT HOW I LET YOU DOWN.

261
00:09:57,514 --> 00:09:58,139
WHAT?

262
00:09:58,181 --> 00:10:00,058
WE GOT A BOX.

263
00:10:04,563 --> 00:10:06,481
I REMEMBER
THE LAST TIME I SAW YOU.

264
00:10:06,523 --> 00:10:08,733
IT WAS THE MORNING
I LEFT FOR COLLEGE

265
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:12,362
AND YOU WERE JUST STANDING
OUTSIDE THE DAIRY QUEEN.

266
00:10:12,404 --> 00:10:16,074
I WAS JUST PROBABLY
WAITING FOR IT TO OPEN.

267
00:10:16,116 --> 00:10:18,034
GOT TO TELL YOU,
YOU LOOK GREAT NOW.

268
00:10:18,076 --> 00:10:20,954
YOU LOOK GREAT, TOO.

269
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,663
YOU'RE AN EXCELLENT PATIENT.

270
00:10:24,291 --> 00:10:25,666
SO HOW DOES IT LOOK?

271
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:27,752
YOU'VE GOT A LITTLE SCRATCH
ON YOUR CORNEA.

272
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:29,796
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
TO WEAR A PATCH.

273
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,798
LIKE A PIRATE?

274
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,674
IF THAT HELPS YOU.

275
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:36,970
OOH.

276
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:38,263
( clears throat )

277
00:10:38,305 --> 00:10:41,224
SO HOW LONG YOU BEEN WORKING
WITH YOUR DAD?

278
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:44,978
COME ON. ONE OF US
HAD TO MENTION HIM.

279
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:48,940
I MOVED BACK HERE
A COUPLE MONTHS AGO.

280
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:50,942
BIG FAMILY
DINNER TONIGHT?

281
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,569
UH, HERE.

282
00:10:52,611 --> 00:10:53,653
OH, NO WAY.

283
00:10:53,694 --> 00:10:55,280
I WAS GOING TO
HAVE THANKSGIVING

284
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:56,406
AT MY GIRLFRIEND'S...

285
00:10:56,448 --> 00:10:57,324
OH.

286
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:59,326
BUT WE BROKE UP.

287
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,161
OH?

288
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:03,580
SHE-SHE WASN'T READY
FOR A SERIOUS COMMITMENT.

289
00:11:03,622 --> 00:11:06,166
OH...

290
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,666
( gruffly ):
SO YOU MADE HER

291
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:09,794
WALK THE PLANK, AYE, MATEY?

292
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:12,464
YOU'RE NOT WEARING
THE PATCH YET.

293
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,675
I KNOW.

294
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:24,934
HE'S COMING HERE
FOR THANKSGIVING?

295
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:26,436
I KNOW. IT'S SICK.

296
00:11:26,478 --> 00:11:27,728
WHY'S IT SICK?

297
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,564
BECAUSE IT'S RICHARD'S SON.

298
00:11:29,606 --> 00:11:32,275
IT'S LIKE INVITING
A GREEK TRAGEDY OVER FOR DINNER.

299
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,568
I MEAN, COME
ON, PHOEBE.

300
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:35,694
YOU UNDERSTAND,
DON'T YOU?

301
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,280
YEAH, I COULD SEE

302
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:40,325
WHERE I'D BE
YOUR BEST SHOT, BUT NO.

303
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:41,784
NO, I'M SORRY, HONEY.

304
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,495
I THINK IT'S TWISTED.

305
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:44,579
WHAT'S TWISTED?

306
00:11:44,621 --> 00:11:46,705
ME GOING OUT
WITH RICHARD'S SON.

307
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:48,458
EWW!

308
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:51,461
EWW, EWW, EWW!

309
00:11:51,503 --> 00:11:53,004
Chandler:
SOUNDS LIKE

310
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:54,713
A REALLY BAD
IDEA TO ME.

311
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:58,759
IS HE OKAY
IN THERE?

312
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:01,346
( firmly ):
HE'S FINE.

313
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:02,847
HEY, YOU KNOW, MON

314
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:05,141
IF THINGS WORK OUT
BETWEEN YOU AND RICHARD'S SON

315
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:06,976
YOU'D BE ABLE TO TELL YOUR KIDS

316
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:09,270
THAT YOU SLEPT
WITH THEIR GRANDFATHER.

317
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:11,898
FINE. JUDGE ALL YOU WANT TO

318
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,233
BUT MARRIED A LESBIAN

319
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:15,151
LEFT A MAN
AT THE ALTAR

320
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:16,861
FELL IN LOVE WITH
A GAY ICE DANCER

321
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:18,821
THREW A GIRL'S WOODEN LEG
IN THE FIRE

322
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:20,114
LIVE IN A BOX!

323
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:30,208
SO, NOW, WHAT EXACTLY
IS THE POINT OF THE BOX?

324
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,502
CHANDLER?

325
00:12:32,544 --> 00:12:35,589
THE MEANING OF THE BOX
IS THREEFOLD.

326
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,632
ONE:

327
00:12:37,674 --> 00:12:40,218
IT GIVES ME THE TIME
TO THINK ABOUT WHAT I DID.

328
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,053
TWO:

329
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:43,638
IT PROVES
HOW MUCH I CARE

330
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,682
ABOUT MY FRIENDSHIP
WITH JOEY.

331
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:47,517
AND THREE:

332
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:50,019
IT HURTS.

333
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,522
OH, HEY.

334
00:12:52,564 --> 00:12:54,941
HEY, UH, DO YOU REMEMBER
THAT NECKLACE

335
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:56,234
I GAVE YOU LAST YEAR?

336
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:57,694
CAN I SEE IT?

337
00:12:58,737 --> 00:13:00,238
WHY?

338
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:01,698
I WANT TO CHECK SOMETHING.

339
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,491
OKAY.

340
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:09,706
NOW WE'LL SEE.

341
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:11,165
AIR HOLE! AIR HOLE!

342
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:12,292
SORRY.

343
00:13:13,627 --> 00:13:15,336
HERE IT IS. I LOVE IT.

344
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:17,046
I WEAR IT
ALL THE TIME.

345
00:13:19,424 --> 00:13:22,093
THE NECKLACE
I GOT YOU WAS GOLD.

346
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:23,637
THIS IS SILVER.

347
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:25,639
HUH.

348
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:29,058
WELL, MAYBE IT, UH...

349
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:30,727
IT CHANGED.

350
00:13:30,769 --> 00:13:32,270
OH, MY GOD.

351
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:34,314
YOU ACTUALLY EXCHANGED IT.

352
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:36,190
ISN'T IT BETTER
THAT I EXCHANGE IT

353
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:37,567
FOR SOMETHING
THAT I ENJOY

354
00:13:37,609 --> 00:13:39,319
AND CAN GET A LOT
OF USE OUT OF?

355
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:43,114
WHAT DID YOU GET?
CREDIT.

356
00:13:43,156 --> 00:13:45,408
( knock at door )

357
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:48,787
I'LL GET IT. I'LL GET IT.
I'LL GET IT. I'LL GET IT.

358
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:53,374
HI, TIM.

359
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:54,626
HI.

360
00:13:54,668 --> 00:13:55,669
HI. THANK YOU.

361
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,170
MEET MY FRIENDS.

362
00:13:57,211 --> 00:13:59,005
THIS IS, UH, PHOEBE.

363
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,214
HI. NICE TO MEET YOU.

364
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:01,257
AND JOEY.

365
00:14:01,299 --> 00:14:03,134
HEY.
MY BROTHER, ROSS.

366
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:04,010
HEY.

367
00:14:04,051 --> 00:14:05,052
AND RACHEL.

368
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:08,640
( Chandler clears throat )

369
00:14:08,682 --> 00:14:10,433
THAT'S CHANDLER.

370
00:14:10,475 --> 00:14:11,934
HOW DO YOU DO?

371
00:14:13,687 --> 00:14:14,937
WHAT'S...?

372
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:16,147
WELL, HE'S, UM...

373
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:18,650
HE'S DOING SOME THINKING.

374
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:22,487
Commentator:
McCallister tries...

375
00:14:22,529 --> 00:14:23,904
YEAH!
YES!

376
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,948
Chandler:
WHAT HAPPENED? WHAT HAPPENED?

377
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,826
YOU KISSED
MY GIRLFRIEND.

378
00:14:31,663 --> 00:14:33,122
OOH, I LIKE
THOSE SUNGLASSES.

379
00:14:33,164 --> 00:14:34,541
"LIKE THEM" LIKE THEM

380
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:37,251
OR "I'D LIKE TO GET STORE CREDIT
FOR THAT AMOUNT"

381
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:39,504
LIKE THEM?

382
00:14:39,546 --> 00:14:41,964
VA FA A NAPOLI.

383
00:14:45,301 --> 00:14:47,595
ALL RIGHT, EVERYBODY;
THIS TURKEY IS READY.

384
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:49,347
WHERE CAN I WASH UP?

385
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:51,140
HERE. LET ME SHOW YOU.

386
00:14:51,182 --> 00:14:54,101
OKAY, THE TOWELS ARE HANGING
NEXT TO THE SINK

387
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:56,563
AND YOU CAN USE
THE FANCY SOAP.

388
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:58,147
THANK YOU.

389
00:14:58,189 --> 00:14:59,649
"FANCY SOAP"?

390
00:14:59,691 --> 00:15:02,151
I THOUGHT WE WERE
SAVING THAT FOR THE POPE.

391
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:03,611
SEE? HE'S NICE, RIGHT?

392
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:05,196
BUT DO YOU REALLY WANT

393
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:07,906
TO BE IN A RELATIONSHIP
WHERE YOU CAN USE THE PHRASE

394
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:10,326
"THAT'S NOT HOW YOUR DAD
USED TO DO IT"?

395
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,208
WOW. EVERYTHING
LOOKS GREAT.

396
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,626
WHERE SHOULD I SIT?

397
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:20,002
SAVED YOU A SEAT.

398
00:15:20,044 --> 00:15:23,339
SICK, SICK, SICK,
SICK, SICK.

399
00:15:23,381 --> 00:15:25,258
( knock at door )

400
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:26,718
OH, I'LL GET IT.

401
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,135
Chandler:
GOTCHA!

402
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:30,889
( laughing )

403
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:34,183
THAT DOESN'T SOUND
LIKE THINKING TO ME.

404
00:15:34,225 --> 00:15:35,685
SORRY.

405
00:15:35,727 --> 00:15:37,645
I DON'T THINK YOU
SHOULD BE TALKING AT ALL.

406
00:15:37,687 --> 00:15:39,689
I THINK YOU GOT
TOO MUCH THINKING TO DO

407
00:15:39,731 --> 00:15:41,274
TO BE TALKING
AND MAKING JOKES.

408
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:42,817
OKAY, OKAY. YOU GOT IT.

409
00:15:42,859 --> 00:15:44,819
ROSS, COULD YOU
PASS ME THE YAMS?

410
00:15:44,861 --> 00:15:46,987
OH, AND JOEY'S GOT
THE MASHED POTATOES

411
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:48,865
IF YOU WANT TO EXCHANGE THEM.

412
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:55,747
WILL YOU STOP?
WHAT IS THE MATTER WITH YOU?

413
00:15:55,789 --> 00:15:57,540
( fake laugh ):
OH, WE'VE GOT COMPANY.

414
00:15:59,626 --> 00:16:01,836
THERE'S NOTHING
THE MATTER WITH ME.

415
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:04,380
SEE, I'M NOT COMPLETELY DEVOID
OF SENTIMENT.

416
00:16:04,422 --> 00:16:06,006
SEE, I HAVE FEELINGS.

417
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:09,135
OKAY, FINE.

418
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:17,769
YOU CAN'T TELL, BUT I'M TRYING
TO BREAK THE TENSION

419
00:16:17,811 --> 00:16:20,187
BY MOONING YOU GUYS.

420
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:24,859
ALL RIGHT, LOOK.

421
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:28,112
IF THIS IS JUST A BIG JOKE
TO YOU, THEN FORGET ABOUT IT.

422
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:29,823
ALL RIGHT,
THIS MEANS SOMETHING TO ME.

423
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,908
IF IT DOESN'T MEAN ANYTHING
TO YOU

424
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:34,285
THEN YOU SHOULD GET
OUT OF THERE.

425
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:36,621
OTHERWISE, YOU'RE JUST
AN IDIOT IN A BOX.

426
00:16:36,663 --> 00:16:38,957
YOU'RE RIGHT,
AND I'M SORRY.

427
00:16:38,997 --> 00:16:40,750
THIS MEANS
A LOT TO ME.

428
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:42,919
I WANT YOU TO BE
MY FRIEND AGAIN.

429
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:45,129
I SWEAR I WON'T
SAY ANOTHER
WORD TONIGHT.

430
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:48,048
SO YOU'RE GOING TO START
TAKING THIS THING SERIOUSLY?

431
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:49,216
ABSOLUTELY.

432
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:51,010
THAT SOUNDS LIKE
ANOTHER WORD TO ME.

433
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:54,806
ARE YOU GOING
TO TAKE THIS SERIOUSLY?

434
00:16:58,476 --> 00:17:00,019
OKAY.

435
00:17:02,355 --> 00:17:05,358
DON'T SAY
THAT I HAVE NO SENTIMENT.

436
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:09,153
THIS IS A MOVIE STUB
FROM OUR FIRST DATE.

437
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:10,655
THIS IS AN EGGSHELL

438
00:17:10,697 --> 00:17:13,491
FROM THE FIRST TIME YOU
MADE ME BREAKFAST IN BED.

439
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:15,326
THIS IS FROM THE MUSEUM

440
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:17,537
THE FIRST TIME...

441
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:19,914
WE WERE TOGETHER.

442
00:17:19,956 --> 00:17:21,749
OKAY, MAYBE

443
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:23,334
I EXCHANGE
GIFTS SOMETIMES

444
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:26,128
BUT I KEEP THE
THINGS THAT MATTER.

445
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,797
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO SAY.

446
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:29,716
I'M SORRY.

447
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,092
THOUGH...

448
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:34,428
YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED
TO TAKE THESE.

449
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,809
IT'S, LIKE,
A MILLION YEARS OLD.

450
00:17:39,851 --> 00:17:42,061
WE... WE ACTUALLY...

451
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:44,355
WE HAVE PEOPLE
LOOKING FOR THAT.

452
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:51,070
OH, THIS ALWAYS HAPPENS.

453
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:53,113
HERE. LET ME, UM...

454
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,073
THANK YOU.

455
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,914
YOU HAVE VERY BEAUTIFUL...

456
00:18:00,955 --> 00:18:02,122
EYE.

457
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,753
YOU KNOW, MY FRIENDS
ALL THINK THIS IS WEIRD.

458
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,838
I THOUGHT IT WAS
GOING TO BE WEIRD.

459
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,549
I ALMOST CALLED TO CANCEL,
BUT IT REALLY ISN'T.

460
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,634
I KNOW. IT'S LIKE
YOU AND YOUR DAD--

461
00:18:13,676 --> 00:18:15,469
THAT'S A TOTALLY
SEPARATE THING.

462
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:18,180
OH, I TOTALLY AGREE.

463
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,600
WE'RE JUST TWO PEOPLE
WHO FIND EACH OTHER...

464
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:23,143
VERY ATTRACTIVE.

465
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:25,021
RIGHT?

466
00:18:34,864 --> 00:18:36,282
WHAT?

467
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:38,952
NOTHING. NOTHING.

468
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:41,704
NO. NO, REALLY--
WAS THAT NOT OKAY?

469
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:43,289
NO, NO, NO, NO.
THAT WAS GOOD.

470
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,415
THAT WAS, UH...

471
00:18:44,457 --> 00:18:46,626
THAT WAS A GOOD KISS.

472
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,669
MY GOD. IT DIDN'T
REMIND YOU OF MY...?

473
00:18:48,711 --> 00:18:50,630
OH, DON'T SAY IT!

474
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:52,256
NO, BUT IT DID,
DIDN'T IT?

475
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:53,674
YES!
OH, MAN!

476
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:54,801
( groaning )

477
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:56,260
I KNOW!

478
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:58,972
( both shudder loudly )

479
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:02,516
Commentator:
...that's 18 yards.

480
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:03,810
Is he having quite a day.

481
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:04,894
( loud shudder )

482
00:19:04,936 --> 00:19:06,062
( knock at door )

483
00:19:06,104 --> 00:19:07,354
I GOT IT.

484
00:19:11,776 --> 00:19:12,902
OH.

485
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:14,570
HEY.

486
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:15,905
HEY.

487
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:18,157
LISTEN. I WANT YOU TO KNOW
HOW SORRY I AM...

488
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,200
THAT'S OKAY.

489
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:22,369
CHANDLER'S THE ONE
I'M MAD AT, SO...

490
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:25,748
WELL, I'M STILL SORRY.

491
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:27,416
IS HE HERE?

492
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:28,960
IN THE BOX.

493
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:33,631
HI.

494
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:37,969
CHANDLER?

495
00:19:38,011 --> 00:19:40,763
OH, HE CAN'T TALK
RIGHT NOW.

496
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:41,973
WHY NOT?

497
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:43,016
WHAT'S GOING ON?

498
00:19:43,057 --> 00:19:44,642
HE'S TRYING
TO SHOW JOEY

499
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:46,226
HOW MUCH
HE MEANS TO HIM.

500
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:48,729
BY BEING IN A BOX.

501
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:50,523
JOEY HAD REASONS.

502
00:19:51,691 --> 00:19:53,442
THEY WERE THREEFOLD.

503
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:58,197
OH. WELL, UH...

504
00:19:58,238 --> 00:19:59,949
YOU NOT BEING
ABLE TO TALK

505
00:19:59,991 --> 00:20:01,993
MIGHT ACTUALLY
MAKE THIS EASIER.

506
00:20:02,035 --> 00:20:04,787
LISTEN, UM...

507
00:20:13,671 --> 00:20:15,173
LISTEN.

508
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,299
I DON'T WANT TO BE SOMEONE

509
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:21,762
WHO COMES
BETWEEN TWO BEST FRIENDS.

510
00:20:21,804 --> 00:20:25,516
I JUST... I CAN'T STAND SEEING
WHAT THIS IS DOING TO YOU GUYS

511
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:27,894
AND I DON'T WANT TO BE
THE CAUSE OF THAT.

512
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:32,190
SO... I DON'T THINK
WE CAN SEE EACH OTHER ANYMORE.

513
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,774
I'M GOING TO GO

514
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:35,776
TO MY MOM'S
IN CHICAGO.

515
00:20:35,818 --> 00:20:38,112
I'M GOING TO STAY THERE
FOR A WHILE.

516
00:20:43,534 --> 00:20:47,080
I THINK THIS COULD HAVE BEEN
SOMETHING REALLY AMAZING.

517
00:20:47,121 --> 00:20:48,414
( laughs softly )

518
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:51,918
BUT, YOU KNOW,
THIS IS PROBABLY FOR THE BEST.

519
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:54,212
YOU KNOW?

520
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:00,885
I'M GOING TO MISS YOU.

521
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:05,639
GOOD-BYE, CHANDLER.

522
00:21:12,730 --> 00:21:15,233
( door closes )

523
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,734
( moaning ):
OPEN THE BOX!

524
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:19,112
Rachel:
WHAT?

525
00:21:19,153 --> 00:21:20,821
HE CAN STILL CATCH HER!

526
00:21:20,863 --> 00:21:22,865
HEY, COME ON.
GET OUT OF THERE!

527
00:21:22,907 --> 00:21:24,825
GET OUT OF THERE!

528
00:21:24,867 --> 00:21:26,077
SO...?

529
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:28,121
YEAH, WE'RE GOING
TO BE FINE. GET OUT.

530
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:31,290
YEAH?

531
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:34,168
YEAH. YOU DID SOME
REAL GOOD THINKING IN THERE.

532
00:21:34,210 --> 00:21:36,087
I MEAN, THIS IS...

533
00:21:36,129 --> 00:21:38,172
( mumbles )

534
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:42,969
NOW, GO 'CAUSE YOU
CAN STILL CATCH HER

535
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,930
AND MERRY CHRISTMAS
FROM YOUR SECRET SANTA!

536
00:21:49,183 --> 00:21:52,394
ALL RIGHT, WHO GOT CHANDLER,
'CAUSE I NEED TO TRADE.

537
00:21:58,317 --> 00:22:00,402
OH, HE SEES HER.

538
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:03,948
OH, HE'S CATCHING
UP TO HER.

539
00:22:03,990 --> 00:22:06,200
OH, SHE SEES HIM.

540
00:22:06,242 --> 00:22:07,660
OH, THEY'RE HUGGING.

541
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:08,702
OHH.

542
00:22:09,954 --> 00:22:13,124
HE'S TAKING
HER PURSE.

543
00:22:13,166 --> 00:22:15,251
UH, THAT'S
NOT THEM.

544
00:22:15,293 --> 00:22:17,128
I'M GOING TO GO
CALL THE POLICE.

545
00:22:19,964 --> 00:22:20,798
OH, THERE THEY ARE!

546
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:22,175
WHERE? OH...

547
00:22:22,216 --> 00:22:24,051
( all sighing )

548
00:22:28,514 --> 00:22:30,516
ALL RIGHT,
GET A ROOM.

